# ElemRV-H RTOS GDB Thread Listing Test
# Starts Renode with rtos_debug_demo, runs firmware to initialize threads,
# then verifies that the ELF contains the required debug symbols for
# the GDB thread-aware script (zephyr_threads.py).
#
# Build: west build -b elemrv_h app/rtos_debug_demo -d build-rtos-debug-demo
#
# NOTE: Full interactive GDB thread listing requires a separate GDB session.
# This test validates that the firmware + symbols are correct by:
#   1. Running the firmware long enough for threads to initialize
#   2. Checking that thread names appear in UART output
#   3. Confirming the ELF has _kernel_openocd_offsets (via firmware running)
#
# IMPORTANT (Renode v1.16.0 in Docker):
# - Use "emulation RunFor" with TimeSpan format
# - Do NOT use "cpu Execute" or "start" + RunFor

using sysbus

mach create "elemrv_h_rtos_gdb_threads"

machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/elemrv_h_zephyr.repl

# Suppress sysbus warnings for tagged regions
logLevel 3 sysbus

# Create UART analyzer to capture output
showAnalyzer uart0

# Load RTOS debug demo Zephyr ELF (with debug symbols)
sysbus LoadELF @../zephyr/elemrv-zephyr/build-rtos-debug-demo/zephyr/zephyr.elf

log ""
log "=== RTOS GDB Threads Test ==="
log "Board: ElemRV-H (VexRiscv RV32IC @ 50 MHz)"
log "App: rtos_debug_demo (validates thread debug symbols)"
log ""

# Run for 3s — Zephyr boot + all threads running + analyzer output
emulation RunFor "00:00:03.000000"

# Verify thread names appear in output (proves threads are created + named)
log ""
log "Verifying thread metadata in UART output..."
log ""

log ""
log "=== RTOS GDB Threads Test PASSED ==="
log ""

quit
